> The discovery? Magic resistance does not protect against a Master
> Lich's Destroy Armor spell. Goodbye +7 Elven Helm!

It does, actually, just not perfectly.  Destroy Armor works as follows:

-- If you do NOT have magic resistance, selects a (weighted) piece of
armor and applies 1-3 levels of erosion to it, also removing any
fooproofing.
-- If you DO have magic resistance, same as above but only applies 1
level.

If the spell targets a piece of armor that is _currently_ "thoroughly"
eroded, then it will be destroyed regardless of MR.  "slightly" and
"very" will be taken to "thoroughly" and stop there, for the non-MR
case.  (moot in the MR case).

